Hello, my name is Anthony Udokwu. I'm the founder of CivTech Allocat, a grant assessment and case management platform I designed and built while leading my UK-registered charity over the past five years.

Most grant management systems focus on processing applications and issuing decisions. Once an applicant is rejected, communication often ends there.

After assessing thousands of applications, I repeatedly encountered appeals, eligibility disputes, requests for clarification, and applicants seeking explanations about decisions. I realised there wasn't a platform designed to manage that part of the process in a structured, transparent, and accountable way.

So I built CivTech Allocat.

The platform supports the complete assessment lifecycle—from application submission and eligibility verification to assessment, decision-making, communication, and post-decision case management.

One of its key features is giving applicants continued access to their records. They can securely log in to:

View submitted applications
See assessment outcomes and decision notes
Access decision rationales
Review previous communications
Submit support requests, complaints, clarification requests, corrections, reviews, or payment enquiries

This functionality is available to both successful and unsuccessful applicants because accountability shouldn't end with a decision.

For administrators, the platform provides workflow automation for application assessment, document verification, interview management, beneficiary administration, audit logging, reporting, and communication management.

Over the past five years, the platform has supported the management of more than 10,000 applications and 30,000 operational records, helping improve transparency, operational efficiency, and trust throughout our programmes.

Thank you for watching.
